STM32F407: MCU

The STM32F407 is a 32-bit microcontroller used in industrial control, motor drives, robotics,
and real-time embedded systems.


1.1 STM32 Family Overview
The STM32F407 uses the Cortex-M4F implementation, which includes a single-precision floating 
point unit (FPU) and DSP instructions. 

For example: the FPU can accelerate floating-point calculations in a motor control algorithm.
An FPU helps a microcontroller perform the decimal-number calculations used in motor control 
faster and more efficiently.

Understanding STM32F407VGT6
a. STM32: STMicroelectronics Microcontroller Family
b. F4: STM32F4 Series, based on Cortex-M4
c. 07: Device Variant within the F4 Family
d. V: 100 pin package
e. G: 1 MB Flash Memory
f. T6: LQFP package, temperature-grade code (6: -40 deg C to +85 deg C)



Internal Architecture


							    Cortex-M4 CPU
				   	   (Registers | ALU | FPU | DSP)
					                ↓ ↑
					          AHB Bus/Bus Matrix 
		   (Connects the CPU, Memory, and High-Speed Bus Masters)
		             ↓ ↑                            ↓ ↑
		        Flash | SRAM                   AHB Peripherals
		  (Program and Data Storage)       (DMA, GPIO-Related Bus Access)
		  							↓ ↑
		  					  APB1/APB2 Buses
		  		 (Timers, USART, SPI, I2C, ADC Interfaces)

The CPU talks to peripherals through bushes. There are fast buses (AHB) and slower ones (APB).
Knowing which bus a peripheral sits on tells you which RCC register enables it clock and what 
clock speed it runs at. This is critical for baud rates and timer math later.
		  
		  
		  
		  
		  
		  
		  
		  
		  
		                          
		             